This product is an Angular adapter for the @docx-editor.dev engine and is a
derivative work of docx-editor:

    docx-editor
    Copyright 2026 EigenPal Inc.
    https://github.com/eigenpal/docx-editor
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The following parts of this repository are derived from that project, in whole
or in part:

  - projects/ng-docx-editor/src/lib/core/deferred-notifier.ts
    Ported from packages/react/src/editor/deferred-notifier.ts. The scheduling
    policy (coalescing, microtask flush, yield to a task under input pressure)
    is part of the engine's behaviour contract and is reproduced deliberately.

  - projects/ng-docx-editor/src/lib/components/toolbar/*
  - projects/ng-docx-editor/src/lib/components/menu/*
  - projects/ng-docx-editor/src/lib/core/chrome-registry.ts
  - projects/ng-docx-editor/src/lib/core/labels.ts
  - projects/ng-docx-editor/src/lib/core/zoom.ts
    The Angular chrome is a port of the React adapter's chrome. Control
    arrangement, labels, icons, enabled-state rules, zoom ladder and colour
    palettes follow that implementation, translated to Angular templates and
    signals, and driven by the shared chrome registry in @docx-editor.dev/core.

  - projects/demo/public/sample.docx
    The sample document shipped with the upstream examples (Apache-2.0).

The engine itself (@docx-editor.dev/core, @docx-editor.dev/i18n,
@docx-editor.dev/fonts) is consumed as a published npm dependency and is not
vendored here. Its license is Apache-2.0 and its own notices travel with the
package.

This repository ships no code from packages/editor-api/, packages/pro/,
packages/docx-to-pdf/ or packages/telemetry/, which are governed by the
EigenPal Pro Evaluation License 1.0 upstream.
